y Park Primary SchoolCurriculum - Boorley Park Primary School","section":"curriculum"},{"text":"Music Curriculum Map Year R Core Text Progression Early Learning Goal - Expressive Arts and Design Being imaginative and expressive Autumn - Positive Role Models: Strengthening Community \u25cf Invent, adapt and recount narratives and stories with peers and their teacher.","sourceUrl":"https://www.boorleypark.org/assets/Uploads/Music-Curriculum-Map-compressed.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"Music Curriculum Map compressed","section":"curriculum"},{"text":"The Arts at Boorley + Community The D@rt Wildern Leisure Centre The Berry Theatre Get into Teaching Staff Vacancies Get Into Teaching Fareham & Gosport","sourceUrl":"https://www.boorleypark.org","sourceType":"school-website","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"Boorley Park Primary SchoolHome - Boorley Park Primary School","section":"homepage"}],"narrativeSummary":"The school website lists drama, drama groups, computing, music, ai in computing. Information appears across 3 pages.","synthesisMethod":"deterministic"},{"area":"ethos","score":73,"confidence":0.71,"summary":"Strong publicly visible evidence for ethos and values (6 specific items). Themes include community, ethos, kindness, moral.","themes":["community","ethos","kindness","moral","nurturing","proud","safe","values","welcoming"],"offerings":[],"signals":[{"text":"For example, the Autumn Term focuses on Positive Role Models and Strengthening Community, with children learning the values of team work, social responsibility and kindness.","sourceUrl":"https://www.boorleypark.org/our-learning/curriculum/","sourceType":"school-website","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"Boorley Park Primary SchoolCurriculum - Boorley Park Primary School","section":"curriculum"},{"text":"Throughout their time with us, children are provided with inspiring learning experiences, which ignite passions, promote diversity and inclusion and support children in being active participants who take moral responsibility in society and the local community.","sourceUrl":"https://www.boorleypark.org","sourceType":"school-website","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"Boorley Park Primary SchoolHome - Boorley Park Primary School","section":"homepage"},{"text":"This includes spreading kindness out in the community, welcoming the community to the school for events and ensuring that everyone feels safe and able to thrive.","sourceUrl":"https://www.boorleypark.org","sourceType":"school-website","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"Boorley Park Primary SchoolHome - Boorley Park Primary School","section":"homepage"},{"text":"Future Focused Fridays This term, we have begun our cross-phase Future Focused Fridays, giving children the opportunity to develop life skills and supporting our ethos of Strengthening Community, Inspiring Minds and Nurturing Futures.","sourceUrl":"https://www.boorleypark.org/our-learning/curriculum/future-focused-fridays/","sourceType":"school-website","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"Boorley Park Primary SchoolFuture Focused Fridays - Boorley Park Primary School","section":"curriculum"},{"text":"Our foundation subjects are taught discretely, but linking to our key concepts: Autumn: Positive Role Models (Strengthening Community) Spring: Innovation (Inspiring Minds) Summer: Sustainability (Nurturing Futures) These key concepts were introduced in September 2025, and our curriculum has been shaped around these.","sourceUrl":"https://www.boorleypark.org/our-learning/curriculum/curriculum-subjects/","sourceType":"school-website","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"Boorley Park Primary SchoolFoundation Subjects - Boorley Park Primary School","section":"curriculum"}],"narrativeSummary":"For example, the Autumn Term focuses on Positive Role Models and Strengthening Community, with children learning the values of team work, social responsibility and kindness.","synthesisMethod":"deterministic"}